type: software
title: "endolift: a scenario-decomposed branch-and-cut with linked lifted cuts for facility location with decision-dependent scenario probabilities"
authors:
  - family-names: Martin
    given-names: Karyamsetty
    email: karyamsettymartin@gmail.com
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-03
license: MIT
keywords:
  - stochastic programming
  - facility location
  - decision-dependent uncertainty
  - endogenous probabilities
  - branch-and-cut
  - lifted cuts
  - RLT
abstract: >-
  C++ branch-and-cut for two-stage stochastic facility location in which the scenario
  probabilities are affine in the opening decision. The relaxation is a linked lifted-cut
  master (Benders cuts of each scenario multiplied by the posiform factors of the probability
  and lifted to pair variables, tied by level-1 RLT linking rows), evaluated by a scenario
  decomposition with closed-form blocks. Includes the instance generator, McCormick baselines
  in the same tree code, an MPI node-parallel tree, a sparse-influence variant, every
  experiment of the paper and the paper itself.
